---[Custom snapshot and AMI policies only] Specifies a retention rule for snapshots created by snapshot policies, or for AMIs created by AMI policies.
---@class aws.dlm.RetainRule
---@field Count? aws.dlm.StandardTierRetainRuleCount The number of snapshots to retain for each volume, up to a maximum of 1000. For example if you want to retain a maximum of three snapshots, specify 3. When the fourth snapshot is created, the oldest retained snapshot is deleted, or it is moved to the archive tier if you have specified an ArchiveRule.
---@field Interval? aws.dlm.StandardTierRetainRuleInterval The amount of time to retain each snapshot. The maximum is 100 years. This is equivalent to 1200 months, 5200 weeks, or 36500 days.
---@field IntervalUnit? aws.dlm.RetentionIntervalUnitValues|string The unit of time for time-based retention. For example, to retain snapshots for 3 months, specify Interval=3 and IntervalUnit=MONTHS. Once the snapshot has been retained for 3 months, it is deleted, or it is moved to the archive tier if you have specified an ArchiveRule.

---[Custom snapshot policies only] Describes the retention rule for archived snapshots. Once the archive retention threshold is met, the snapshots are permanently deleted from the archive tier.
---@class aws.dlm.RetentionArchiveTier
---@field Count? aws.dlm.Count The maximum number of snapshots to retain in the archive storage tier for each volume. The count must ensure that each snapshot remains in the archive tier for at least 90 days. For example, if the schedule creates snapshots every 30 days, you must specify a count of 3 or more to ensure that each snapshot is archived for at least 90 days.
---@field Interval? aws.dlm.Interval Specifies the period of time to retain snapshots in the archive tier. After this period expires, the snapshot is permanently deleted.
---@field IntervalUnit? aws.dlm.RetentionIntervalUnitValues|string The unit of time in which to measure the Interval. For example, to retain a snapshots in the archive tier for 6 months, specify Interval=6 and IntervalUnit=MONTHS.

---@alias aws.dlm.RetentionIntervalUnitValues "DAYS"|"WEEKS"|"MONTHS"|"YEARS"

---[Custom snapshot and AMI policies only] Specifies a schedule for a snapshot or AMI lifecycle policy.
---@class aws.dlm.Schedule
---@field Name? aws.dlm.ScheduleName The name of the schedule.
---@field CopyTags? aws.dlm.CopyTags Copy all user-defined tags on a source volume to snapshots of the volume created by this policy.
---@field TagsToAdd? aws.dlm.TagsToAddList The tags to apply to policy-created resources. These user-defined tags are in addition to the Amazon Web Services-added lifecycle tags.
---@field VariableTags? aws.dlm.VariableTagsList [AMI policies and snapshot policies that target instances only] A collection of key/value pairs with values determined dynamically when the policy is executed. Keys may be any valid Amazon EC2 tag key. Values must be in one of the two following formats: $(instance-id) or $(timestamp). Variable tags are only valid for EBS Snapshot Management – Instance policies.
---@field CreateRule? aws.dlm.CreateRule The creation rule.
---@field RetainRule? aws.dlm.RetainRule The retention rule for snapshots or AMIs created by the policy.
---@field FastRestoreRule? aws.dlm.FastRestoreRule [Custom snapshot policies only] The rule for enabling fast snapshot restore.
---@field CrossRegionCopyRules? aws.dlm.CrossRegionCopyRules Specifies a rule for copying snapshots or AMIs across Regions.
---@field ShareRules? aws.dlm.ShareRules [Custom snapshot policies only] The rule for sharing snapshots with other Amazon Web Services accounts.
---@field DeprecateRule? aws.dlm.DeprecateRule [Custom AMI policies only] The AMI deprecation rule for the schedule.
---@field ArchiveRule? aws.dlm.ArchiveRule [Custom snapshot policies that target volumes only] The snapshot archiving rule for the schedule. When you specify an archiving rule, snapshots are automatically moved from the standard tier to the archive tier once the schedule's retention threshold is met. Snapshots are then retained in the archive tier for the archive retention period that you specify.

---@alias aws.dlm.ScheduleList aws.dlm.Schedule[]

---@alias aws.dlm.ScheduleName string

---[Custom snapshot policies that target instances only] Information about pre and/or post scripts for a snapshot lifecycle policy that targets instances. For more information, see Automating application-consistent snapshots with pre and post scripts.
---@class aws.dlm.Script
---@field Stages? aws.dlm.StagesList Indicate which scripts Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager should run on target instances. Pre scripts run before Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager initiates snapshot creation. Post scripts run after Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager initiates snapshot creation.
---@field ExecutionHandlerService? aws.dlm.ExecutionHandlerServiceValues|string Indicates the service used to execute the pre and/or post scripts.
---@field ExecutionHandler aws.dlm.ExecutionHandler The SSM document that includes the pre and/or post scripts to run.
---@field ExecuteOperationOnScriptFailure? aws.dlm.ExecuteOperationOnScriptFailure Indicates whether Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager should default to crash-consistent snapshots if the pre script fails.
---@field ExecutionTimeout? aws.dlm.ScriptExecutionTimeout Specifies a timeout period, in seconds, after which Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager fails the script run attempt if it has not completed. If a script does not complete within its timeout period, Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager fails the attempt. The timeout period applies to the pre and post scripts individually.
---@field MaximumRetryCount? aws.dlm.ScriptMaximumRetryCount Specifies the number of times Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager should retry scripts that fail.

---@alias aws.dlm.ScriptExecutionTimeout number

---@alias aws.dlm.ScriptMaximumRetryCount number

